<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatima</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fatima was the daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and wife of Ali. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> took its name from her, as its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> claimed descent from her and Ali, a claim that was central to their religious legitimacy.</p></div>
